 and Russian forts and the location where Russian Alaska was formally handed over to the United States in 1867.","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/American_Flag-Raising_Site_%2820357938078%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","wpu":"Castle Hill (Sitka, Alaska)"},{"n":"Southeast Resort","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":57.051295,"lo":-135.333638,"d":540,"w":"https://southeastresort.com","ph":"+1 907-747-6241","ad":"330 Seward Street","wifi":1},{"n":"Kaisei Maru","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":57.048712,"lo":-135.347763,"d":590},{"n":"Sitka Rose Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":57.051287,"lo":-135.331844,"d":643,"ad":"419 Lincoln Street"},{"n":"Russian Bishops House","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.051428,"lo":-135.331233,"d":674,"ph":"+1 907 7470110","wp":"en:Russian Bishop's House","wd":"Q18391553","ad":"501 Lincoln Street","ds":"The Russian Bishop's House (Russian: Русский Архиерейский Дом), once the Russian Mission Orphanage (Russian: Российская Миссия Орфанадж), is a historic house museum and National Historic Landmark at Lincoln and Monastery Streets in Sitka, Alaska.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Russian_Bishop_House_August_2005.JPG/960px-Russian_Bishop_House_August_2005.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Russian Bishop's House"},{"n":"Sitka History Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.049561,"lo":-135.332005,"d":715,"h":"Mo-Fr 08:00-18:00","w":"https://sitkahistory.com/","ph":"+1 907-738-3766"},{"n":"Sitka Sound Science Center","g":"sights","k":"aquarium","la":57.049777,"lo":-135.323519,"d":1173,"ds":"The Sitka Sound Science Center is a non-profit dedicated to research and education in Alaska in Sitka, Alaska. It is based in the Sage Building, which is located on Lincoln Street across from the old Sheldon Jackson Campus. It is a biological field station and includes the Sheldon Jackson salmon hatchery, the Molly Ahlgren Aquarium, a research lab, classrooms and offices.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Sage_Bldg.jpg/960px-Sage_Bldg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Sitka Sound Science Center"},{"n":"Sage Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":57.049171,"lo":-135.323082,"d":1220},{"n":"Sheldon Jackson Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":57.050525,"lo":-135.322297,"d":1222,"h":"Sep-Apr We-Sa 10:00-16:00; May-Sep Mo-Fr 09:00-16:30; May-Sep Su 13:00-16:30","w":"https://museums.alaska.gov/sheldon_jackson/","ad":"104 College Drive"},{"n":"Sitka National Historical Park","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":57.048637,"lo":-135.3191,"d":1467,"ad":"106 Metlakatla Street","f":["wc"],"ds":"Sitka National Historical Park (earlier known as Indian River Park and Totem Park) is a national historical park in Sitka, Alaska. It was redesignated as a national historical park from its previous status as national monument on October 18, 1972. The park in its various forms has sought to commemorate the Tlingit and Russian experiences in Alaska.","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Native_Alaskan_Totem_Pole.JPG/960px-Native_Alaskan_Totem_Pole.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","wpu":"Sitka National Historical Park"},{"n":"Viewpoint","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":57.067586,"lo":-135.3295,"d":1789},{"n":"Gavan Viewpoint","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":57.072225,"lo":-135.319556,"d":2532},{"n":"Gavan Lookout","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":57.072225,"lo":-135.319556,"d":2532},{"n":"Sandy Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":57.075587,"lo":-135.373236,"d":3142},{"n":"Fort Rousseau (historical)","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":57.039417,"lo":-135.389185,"d":3229},{"n":"Tongass Federal Credit Union","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":57.05367,"lo":-135.336429,"d":345,"ad":"401 Halibut Point Road"},{"n":"Harry Race Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":